# Trivy vulnerability-ignore list for the opensign-client image
# (used via --ignorefile in .github/workflows/opensign-client-rebuild.yml).
#
# WHY THESE ARE ACCEPTED
# The OS layer is NOT ignored: the Dockerfile runs `apt-get dist-upgrade`
# (refreshed every time the base image digest moves -- see
# .opensign-client-base-digest), so the Debian packages ship at their
# latest point-release and the only fixable CRITICAL/HIGH findings left in
# the image are the Node.js application + npm dependencies below. Every one
# is either baked into the pinned node:22.14.0 image (the npm CLI's own
# transitive tree) or pinned by upstream's apps/OpenSign/package-lock.json,
# and each has a newer version on the npm registry that fixes it -- we just
# can't move it without forking OpenSign's dependency tree or floating the
# pinned node:22.14.0 base, both of which this repo deliberately avoids for
# reproducibility.
#
# Lower severities and CVEs with no available fix are reported by Trivy but
# don't block; only fixable CRITICAL/HIGH do (trivy-scan.sh), so a fresh CVE
# in the OS layer or a dependency bump will fail the build until it's either
# patched or explicitly added here with a reason.
#
# Re-check after a node:22.14.0 -> node:X.Y.Z base bump and after each
# OpenSign release: a newer node bundles a newer npm (shrinking the
# node-bundled set) and upstream may have bumped axios / fast-uri / undici.
# Prune ids Trivy no longer reports (stale entries would silently hide a
# regression back to a vulnerable version).

# --- node:22.14.0's bundled npm (the npm CLI's own dependency tree) --------
# brace-expansion 2.0.1
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

